Subject: [PATCH 12/13] docs: B3 design rev 4 - the fix round; the B3 balance
 rows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rev 4 records what the fix round changed (the tourism layer event and slice window, -0, the advisors'
month scans in any list order, EM-1's towns), what it re-verified at 038100b (digests bit-identical to
bed0ebf on both fixtures, tsc and vitest, the bot, the balance procedure), and why the rest is not
changed in B3's files: the full-game save / load gate (pre-existing, in the base too), approval's resumed
init (L7: a tested 4-line approval.ts patch for the lead) and the as-written timing reading (L0 / L1 / L2).

tests/sim/fixtures/balance-baseline.json: the B3 rows (256x60 seeds 7 and 11, 128x15 seed 7, at 038100b)
under a new "b3" key, as §8 asked; the other rows are untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
